# Feed the Herd. — Product Showcase & Admin CMS: Exact Recreation Prompt

Build a single page that recreates a high-end 3D "runway" product showcase section called "Feed the Herd." for a factory livestock feed reference catalog. Six full-size 25kg livestock feed bags (featuring flagship codes **414**, **415**, **418**, alongside **412**, **416**, and **420**) stand on a clean white stage, arranged in depth on a turning 3D ring with blurred outer bags. The carousel advances every 5 seconds, with a 01–06 progress bar, arrows, and a pause button. It has a custom "Drag / View" cursor and a "View bag" popup with numbered specification pins on the packaging.

This page is a **purely informational product showcase (no pricing displayed)**. A right-hand "In this formula" panel lists the 3 core specification pillars (**Target Livestock**, **Suitable Age & Weight**, and **Nutritional Composition**) with plus buttons and technical parameter pickers (Pellet Diameter, Packaging Tier, Formula Premix), ending with a "Factory Quality Standard" summary and a "Save full formula to shortlist" button. A local "product shortlist" dialog keeps the selected reference specs for export.

Additionally, include a **Password-Protected Admin CMS Modal (`ID: admin`, `Password: adminsale`)** accessible from the header. Once authenticated, the Admin can dynamically change any feed bag's packaging image (via image URL or local file upload converted to Data URL), edit bag names, pin coordinates, and customize all 3 specification pillars (Target Livestock, Suitable Age, Nutritional Composition). All Admin changes save to `localStorage` and immediately re-render the 3D stage, clones, heroes, and specification panels without losing the 3D physics.

Write plain HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript with no frameworks. The section is a custom element `<runway-section>` defined with `customElements.define`. Every number in this brief comes from the final source and must be used as given.

