## 5. Layout

### 5.1 Frame and grid (desktop ≥1100px)

- `.rw__sticky` has height `var(--rw-frame-h, 100svh)` and is a flex column. On desktop this is `max(380, innerHeight − 88)`.
- `.rw__grid` is a grid with `grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) 380px` and `grid-template-rows: minmax(0,1fr)`, full width.
- **Left column `.rw__left`**: relative, flex column, background white (stage), `overflow:hidden`. Contains `.rw__head`, `.rw__stage`, `.rw__controls`, and the popup `.rw__lb`.
- **Right column `.rw__panel.has-rule`**: background white, `border-left: 1px solid #c8c8c8`. `.rw__panel-inner` is `position:absolute; inset:0`, a flex column.

### 5.2 Head

- `.rw__head` is flex, `justify-content: space-between`, `align-items: flex-end`, gap 24px, padding `44px 56px 0`, z-index 5.
- `.rw__intro` is a flex column, gap 12px, max-width 640px:
  - `<h2 class="rw__title">Feed the Herd.</h2>`: margin 0, heading family, weight 400, 46px, line-height 1, letter-spacing −0.02em, colour #151413.
  - `<p class="rw__sub">Six precision formulas, engineered for every growth stage. Tap a bag to inspect target livestock, age & nutrition.</p>`: 12px, line-height 1.55, colour #66625c, max-width 46ch.
- Visually hidden live region `<span class="rw__sr" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-rw-live>` announces e.g. `"Look 1: Feed 414 — Grower Pig"` on each change.

### 5.3 Stage

- `.rw__stage[data-rw-stage]` has `tabindex="0" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel"` and `aria-label="Feed the Herd. — use arrow keys or swipe to change feed bag"`.
- Children, in order:
  1. `.rw__actors[data-rw-actors]` with the six `.rw__model` queue bodies (plus six clones appended by script).
  2. `.rw__heroes[data-rw-heroes]` with the six `.rw__hero` elements.
  3. `<span class="rw__sweep">` (light sweep overlay).
  4. `<span class="rw__cursor" data-rw-cursor>` holding `<span class="rw__cursor-in">` with `<span class="rw__cursor-label rw__cursor-drag">Drag</span><span class="rw__cursor-label rw__cursor-view">View</span>`.
  5. `<span class="rw__walk"><span class="rw__walk-line"></span></span>` (phone-only progress line).
- **Queue body, Contact shadow, Hero, and Pins**: Identical DOM structure, CSS classes, aspect-ratio (`--rw-ar: 0.5625`), and radial contact shadow as the reference architecture. Because the section has class `rw--popup`, pins inside the stage heroes are `display:none !important` and appear only inside the "View bag" popup.

